      sources: "Sources: Chapter 03, “Checklist,” “Continue the book”; Learn, Get onPremisesDirectorySynchronization.",
      say: `Here's what a reviewer checks before a new check ships. The name, function and track agree. The catalog names the least privilege and the role straight from Learn, and if that role is privileged, the check is optional and reads an export. It reads only through the shared data path, hides no failed read, and treats every missing control as off. Its fixtures follow Learn's shape, its tests cover every status, the README knows about it, and the safety tests pass untouched. Next up is Chapter 4, dynamic rules as code. Thanks for watching.`,
      detail: `Checklist: the check ID, function name and track agree (VK-SYNC-02, Invoke-VkSync02, SYNC). The catalog entry names the least-privileged permission and the delegated role from the Learn page, and links that page. A check whose read needs a privileged role is optional and reads an export by default. The body reads only through Get-VkData, Read-VkInputJson or Read-VkInputCsv. No try/catch in the body hides a failed read. Every control is read with the unsafe default. Pass and fail fixtures exist, in Learn's response shape, and the table-driven test has the exact fail count. Tests cover each status the check can return. The README's permission table, notes and gate map include the check. The safety tests pass unchanged. Next: Chapter 04 — Dynamic Rules as Code. Previous: Chapter 02 — Graph Clients for the Government Clouds.`,
